{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Getting Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/Examples"]},{"title":"Classes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivitiesImplementationSetup"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivityAttributes","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivityContentState"],"title":"Protocols"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/AnyCodable","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/DefaultLiveActivityAttributes","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivityAttributeData","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivityContentStateData"],"title":"Structures"},{"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshBridge"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PushwooshLiveActivities integrates Apple’s ActivityKit framework to deliver real-time updates to Live Activities on the Lock Screen and Dynamic Island. Live Activities provide persistent, glanceable information that users can track without opening your app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module handles token registration, activity lifecycle management, and push notification delivery automatically. It supports both custom activity attributes and a default configuration for cross-platform scenarios."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshLiveActivities\/documentation\/PushwooshLiveActivities\/PushwooshLiveActivitiesImplementationSetup\/setup(_:)"},{"text":" for every attributes type your app uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"at launch"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)"},{"text":" or the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App.init"},{"type":"text","text":"), not lazily when a screen appears. Only a type registered in the current session is reconnected to its already-running activities so their push token can be re-uploaded after a cold start — for example an activity that started, or was scheduled to start, while the app was terminated. A type registered later (e.g. in a view’s "},{"code":"onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") can’t receive remote updates until that screen is opened. ActivityKit exposes running activities only through the concrete "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Activity<Attributes>"},{"text":" generic and does not persist the set of types across launches, so the SDK cannot reconnect a type it hasn’t been told about this session. The call is idempotent — registering at launch and again per-screen is safe.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Real-time iOS Live Activities powered by push notifications."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/pushwooshliveactivities"]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/pushwooshliveactivities"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"